## Introduction & Overview

### What is DB2?

**DB2 (Database 2)** is IBM's relational database management system (RDBMS) for mainframe environments (z/OS). It provides:
- ACID-compliant transactional database
- High availability and reliability
- Performance optimization for massive data volumes
- Enterprise security and access control
- Seamless integration with CICS and other mainframe applications

### DB2 Characteristics

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│      DB2 CORE FEATURES              │
├─────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ✓ Relational database (RDBMS)       │
│ ✓ ACID compliance                   │
│ ✓ SQL standard support              │
│ ✓ High concurrency                  │
│ ✓ Multi-version concurrency         │
│ ✓ Advanced indexing                 │
│ ✓ 24/7/365 availability            │
│ ✓ Enterprise security               │
│ ✓ Performance monitoring            │
│ ✓ Automated utilities               │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Why DB2?

```
Business Requirements:
├─ Massive data volumes (petabytes)
├─ Concurrent users (millions)
├─ ACID guarantees (no data loss)
├─ Sub-second response times
├─ 99.99%+ availability
└─ Enterprise security

DB2 Provides:
├─ Proven reliability (50+ years)
├─ Unmatched performance
├─ Scalability to petabytes
├─ Industry-standard SQL
├─ Enterprise security model
└─ Built-in recovery mechanisms
