## Architecture

### DB2 System Architecture

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│         Client Applications / CICS          │
│  (Online transaction processing)            │
└──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘
                       │ SQL Queries
┌──────────────────────▼───────────────────────┐
│           DB2 SQL Engine                     │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │  Query Optimizer                       │ │
│  │  (Execution plan selection)            │ │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │  Query Executor                        │ │
│  │  (Execution plan execution)            │ │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │  Buffer Manager                        │ │
│  │  (Memory caching, I/O management)      │ │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │  Lock Manager                          │ │
│  │  (Concurrency control)                 │ │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │  Recovery Manager                      │ │
│  │  (Transaction logging, recovery)       │ │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
     ↓          ↓          ↓          ↓
  Table    Index    Logs       System
  Spaces   Spaces   Catalog    Catalogs
```

### Key Components

#### 1. Storage Structure

```
Tablespace
├─ Collection of tables
├─ Physical allocation unit
├─ Type: Segmented, Partitioned, or Simple
│
├─ Pages (4KB or 8KB or 16KB or 32KB)
│  └─ Basic unit of data storage
│  └─ Contains multiple rows
│
└─ Extents
   └─ Collection of pages
   └─ Allocation unit (disk space)
```

#### 2. Buffer Pool

```
Memory Hierarchy:

CPU L1 Cache (< 1ns)
  ↓
CPU L2 Cache (5-10ns)
  ↓
Main Memory (50-100ns)
  ├─ Buffer Pool
  │  └─ Caches frequently accessed pages
  │  └─ Managed by DB2
  │  └─ Hit rate determines performance
  ↓
Disk (5-10ms)
  └─ Persistent storage
```

#### 3. Log System

```
Transaction Log:
├─ Sequential write (fast)
├─ Every change recorded
├─ Used for recovery
├─ Also for audit trail

Log Structure:
├─ Active logs (current transactions)
├─ Archive logs (completed, kept for recovery)
└─ Backup logs (backup reference)
```

