## Data Types & Storage

### Numeric Data Types

```
Integer Types:
├─ SMALLINT (2 bytes)     -32,768 to 32,767
├─ INTEGER (4 bytes)      -2.1B to 2.1B
└─ BIGINT (8 bytes)       -9.2E18 to 9.2E18

Decimal Types:
├─ DECIMAL(p,s)
│  └─ p = precision (total digits)
│  └─ s = scale (decimal places)
│  └─ Example: DECIMAL(9,2) = 1234567.89
│
├─ NUMERIC (same as DECIMAL)
└─ REAL, DOUBLE (floating point)

Usage:
├─ Integers: IDs, counts, quantities
├─ Decimal: Money, percentages
└─ Float: Scientific calculations
```

### String Data Types

```
Fixed Length:
├─ CHAR(n)
│  └─ Always n bytes
│  └─ Padded with spaces if shorter
│  └─ Good for codes
│  └─ Example: CHAR(2) for state code

Variable Length:
├─ VARCHAR(n) or VARCHAR2(n)
│  └─ Up to n bytes
│  └─ Only stores used space
│  └─ Good for names, addresses
│  └─ Example: VARCHAR(100) for name
│
└─ CLOB (Character Large Object)
   └─ For very large text (100MB+)
   └─ Documents, descriptions
   └─ Requires special handling
```

### Date/Time Data Types

```
DATE:
├─ Stores date only (YYYY-MM-DD)
├─ Example: 2024-12-31
└─ Used for birthdays, order dates

TIME:
├─ Stores time only (HH:MM:SS)
├─ Example: 14:30:45
└─ Used for appointments, schedules

TIMESTAMP:
├─ Stores date AND time
├─ Example: 2024-12-31 14:30:45.123456
├─ Precision to microseconds
└─ Used for transaction timestamps

Usage Functions:
├─ CURRENT_DATE     → Today's date
├─ CURRENT_TIME     → Current time
├─ CURRENT_TIMESTAMP → Date and time
└─ DATE('2024-12-31') → Explicit date
```

