## Security & Access Control

### Authentication

```
User Login Process:

User ID + Password
  ↓
DB2 Authentication
  ├─ RACF (Resource Access Control Facility)
  ├─ LDAP (Lightweight Directory Access)
  └─ Custom authentication
  ↓
Verify Credentials
  ├─ Check in security database
  ├─ Validate password strength
  └─ Check for expired password
  ↓
Establish Connection
  ├─ Create session
  ├─ Assign privileges
  └─ Ready for queries
```

### Authorization

```
Privilege Types:

Object Privileges:
├─ SELECT (read from table)
├─ INSERT (add rows)
├─ UPDATE (modify rows)
├─ DELETE (remove rows)
├─ ALTER (modify table structure)
└─ INDEX (create indexes)

System Privileges:
├─ CREATETAB (create tables)
├─ CREATETS (create tablespaces)
├─ BACKUP (backup database)
├─ CREATEDB (create database)
└─ SYSADM (system administrator)

Row-Level Security:
├─ Restrict rows visible to user
├─ Based on user attributes
├─ Example: Users see only their data
└─ Enforced in WHERE clause
```

### Column-Level Encryption

```
Sensitive Data Protection:

Unencrypted (Risky):
┌────────────────────────────┐
│ CUSTOMER TABLE             │
├────────────────────────────┤
│ NAME | SSN      | SALARY   │
├────────────────────────────┤
│ John | 123-45-6789 | 75000 │
│ Jane | 234-56-7890 | 85000 │
└────────────────────────────┘
(Anyone with database access sees SSNs)

Encrypted:
┌────────────────────────────┐
│ CUSTOMER TABLE             │
├────────────────────────────┤
│ NAME | SSN (Encrypted) | SALARY |
├────────────────────────────┤
│ John | ax9K3$mP2... | 75000 |
│ Jane | bx9K3$mP2... | 85000 │
└────────────────────────────┘
(Only authorized users can decrypt)
```

