## CICS Integration

### Theory: CICS ↔ DB2 Interaction

```
Transaction Flow:

┌──────────────┐
│ CICS Program │
└──────┬───────┘
       │
       ├─ EXEC CICS LINK
       │  └─ Calls database service
       │
       ├─ SQL Query
       │  └─ Sent to DB2
       │
       ├─ DB2 Processing
       │  ├─ Query optimization
       │  ├─ Index lookup
       │  ├─ Data retrieval
       │  └─ Return results
       │
       └─ Program continues
          ├─ Process results
          ├─ Format response
          └─ Send to terminal
```

### Code Example: CICS-DB2 Integration

```cobol
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. CUSTOMER-LOOKUP.

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 WS-CUST-ID           PIC 9(8).
01 WS-CUST-NAME         PIC X(30).
01 WS-CUST-PHONE        PIC X(12).
01 WS-CUST-CREDIT       PIC 9(9)V99.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.

LOOKUP-CUSTOMER.
    PERFORM GET-CUSTOMER-REQUEST.
    PERFORM QUERY-DATABASE.
    PERFORM SEND-RESPONSE.
    STOP RUN.

GET-CUSTOMER-REQUEST.
    EXEC CICS RECEIVE MAP('CUSTMAP')
        MAPSET('CUSTSET')
        INTO(CUSTOMER-REQUEST)
    END-EXEC.
    
    MOVE CUST-ID TO WS-CUST-ID.

QUERY-DATABASE.
    EXEC CICS EXEC SQL
        SELECT NAME, PHONE, CREDIT_LIMIT
        INTO :WS-CUST-NAME, :WS-CUST-PHONE, :WS-CUST-CREDIT
        FROM CUSTOMER
        WHERE CUST_ID = :WS-CUST-ID
    END-EXEC.

SEND-RESPONSE.
    MOVE WS-CUST-NAME TO RESPONSE-NAME.
    MOVE WS-CUST-PHONE TO RESPONSE-PHONE.
    MOVE WS-CUST-CREDIT TO RESPONSE-CREDIT.
    
    EXEC CICS SEND MAP('RESPONSE')
        MAPSET('CUSTSET')
        FROM(RESPONSE-AREA)
        ERASE
    END-EXEC.
```

