## Best Practices

### Design Best Practices

```
1. Normalization
   ├─ 1NF: Remove repeating groups
   ├─ 2NF: Remove partial dependencies
   ├─ 3NF: Remove transitive dependencies
   └─ Reduces redundancy, improves data quality

2. Primary Keys
   ├─ Every table needs one
   ├─ Use surrogate key if no natural key
   ├─ Small (INT preferred over VARCHAR)
   └─ Immutable (never change)

3. Foreign Keys
   ├─ Enforce referential integrity
   ├─ Prevent orphaned records
   ├─ Index foreign key columns
   └─ Use CASCADE delete carefully

4. Column Design
   ├─ Appropriate data types
   ├─ Right sizes (not over/under)
   ├─ Default values where sensible
   └─ NOT NULL for required columns
```

### Performance Best Practices

```
1. Indexing Strategy
   ├─ Index columns in WHERE clauses
   ├─ Index columns in JOIN conditions
   ├─ Avoid too many indexes (>10 per table)
   ├─ Regular index maintenance (REORG, RUNSTATS)
   └─ Monitor and delete unused indexes

2. Query Optimization
   ├─ Use EXPLAIN PLAN regularly
   ├─ Avoid full table scans
   ├─ Use specific column lists (not *)
   ├─ Partition large tables
   └─ Archive old data

3. Transaction Design
   ├─ Keep transactions short
   ├─ Minimize lock hold time
   ├─ Batch similar operations
   ├─ Avoid nested transactions
   └─ Use appropriate isolation levels

4. Memory Management
   ├─ Right buffer pool sizes
   ├─ Monitor cache hit ratio
   ├─ Prefetch settings tuned
   └─ Memory not wasted
```

### Maintenance Best Practices

```
1. Regular Monitoring
   ├─ Query performance metrics
   ├─ Index fragmentation
   ├─ Table growth
   ├─ Lock contention
   └─ Deadlock frequency

2. Scheduled Maintenance
   ├─ REORG (reorganize tables/indexes)
   ├─ RUNSTATS (update statistics)
   ├─ REBUILD (rebuild indexes)
   ├─ BACKUP (daily full, hourly incremental)
   └─ DBCC (database consistency check)

3. Capacity Planning
   ├─ Monitor disk usage
   ├─ Track growth rate
   ├─ Project future needs
   ├─ Plan expansions
   └─ Manage storage costs

4. Documentation
   ├─ Database design documents
   ├─ Query optimization guide
   ├─ Runbooks for operations
   ├─ Disaster recovery procedures
   └─ Security policies
```

