## Troubleshooting Scenarios

### Issue 1: Deadlock Resolution

```
Symptom: Application gets "Deadlock" error

Scenario:
Transaction A:
1. Locks ACCOUNT 100001
2. Tries to lock ACCOUNT 100002

Transaction B:
1. Locks ACCOUNT 100002
2. Tries to lock ACCOUNT 100001

Result: Mutual waiting → DEADLOCK

DB2 Detection:
└─ Timeout after 30 seconds
└─ One transaction aborted
└─ Error returned to application

Application Handling:
EXEC CICS EXEC SQL
    (Transaction logic)
END-EXEC

IF SQLCODE = -911  (Deadlock error)
    PERFORM RETRY-WITH-BACKOFF
END-IF.

Prevention:
├─ Always lock in same order (100001 → 100002)
├─ Minimize lock hold time
├─ Use isolation level COMMITTED READ
└─ Batch similar operations
```

### Issue 2: Out of Memory (Buffer Pool)

```
Symptom: "No more storage available" error

Investigation:
EXEC SQL
    SELECT BPNAME, NPAGES, NFREE
    FROM BUFFER_POOLS
END-EXEC.

Problem Identified:
├─ Buffer pool size: 10GB
├─ Pages allocated: 95%
├─ Free pages: 5% (too low)
├─ Cache hit rate: 60% (should be 85%+)

Root Cause:
└─ Large query doing full table scan
└─ Evicting all data from cache
└─ Cascading effect on other queries

Solution:
1. Increase buffer pool size 10GB → 20GB
   └─ Add more RAM
   └─ Rebuild buffer pools

2. Optimize problematic query
   └─ Add index to force index scan
   └─ Reduce rows processed
   └─ Limit result set

Result:
├─ Cache hit rate: 85%+
├─ Response time: Improved 5x
└─ System stable
```

